@startuml concurrency-model
' liblevenshtein — read/write concurrency model. Every dictionary backend now reads
' LOCK-FREE: a reader never blocks on a writer. Static dicts read immutable arrays;
' dynamic dicts load an ArcSwap snapshot; writers publish new state by an atomic swap / CAS.
' Color legend:
'   concurrency  #CFD8DC (blue-grey)  = grouping banner
'   in-memory    #E8F5E9 (green)      = in-memory backends
'   disk         #E0F2F1 (teal)       = disk-persisted (durable) backends
'   border/arrow #455A64 (slate)
' Grouping is by actual read behaviour. Every in-memory backend reports
' SyncStrategy::InternalSync (PathMap snapshots report Persistent); DoubleArrayTrie
' reports the ExternalSync trait default yet is immutable, so its reads are wait-free.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3E0
  BorderColor #EF6C00
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

title Concurrency model — every dictionary reads lock-free (a reader never blocks a writer)

rectangle "All dictionaries: Send + Sync · Arc cheap-clone · lock-free reads" as banner #CFD8DC

rectangle "In-memory — lock-free / wait-free reads" as gmem #CFD8DC {
  rectangle "DoubleArrayTrie(Char)\nimmutable array · <latex>\mathcal{O}(1)</latex> reads · static (wait-free)" as dat #E8F5E9
  rectangle "DynamicDawg(Char) / DynamicDawgU64\nLockFreeDawg · per-node ArcSwap · CAS writes" as dd #E8F5E9
  rectangle "SuffixAutomaton(Char)\nLockFreeSuffixAutomaton · ArcSwap · substring" as sa #E8F5E9
  rectangle "Scdawg(Char)\nLockFreeScdawg · ArcSwap · bidirectional" as sc #E8F5E9
  rectangle "PathMapDictionary(Char)\nArc<ArcSwap<PathMapState>> · atomic-swap writes" as pmd #E8F5E9
  rectangle "PathMapSnapshot / PathMapRef(Char)\npersistent copy-on-write snapshot" as pms #E8F5E9
  rectangle "BijectiveMap\nlock-free DynamicDawgChar + ArcSwap reverse map" as bij #E8F5E9
}

rectangle "Disk-persisted — durable AND lock-free reads" as gdisk #CFD8DC {
  rectangle "PersistentARTrie(Char / U64)\nlock-free CAS overlay · mmap" as part #E0F2F1
  rectangle "PersistentScdawg / PersistentSuffixAutomaton /\nPersistentSuffixTree(Char)\nArcSwap graph · disk-persisted" as psub #E0F2F1
  rectangle "PersistentVocabARTrie\nlock-free overlay · term ↔ id · disk" as pv #E0F2F1
}

note bottom of gmem
  Every in-memory backend reports SyncStrategy::InternalSync (PathMap snapshots
  report Persistent). Writers publish new state by an atomic ArcSwap swap or a
  compare_exchange CAS and never exclude readers. Earlier releases guarded the
  dynamic backends (DynamicDawg · SuffixAutomaton · Scdawg), PathMapDictionary,
  and BijectiveMap with a parking_lot RwLock; that RwLock now survives only inside
  the disk-backed persistent_artrie engine, never on a dictionary read path.
end note

banner -[#455A64,thickness=3]down-> gmem
banner -[#455A64,thickness=3]down-> gdisk

@enduml
